{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Has His grace failed forever?</b> — Like <i>ki ephes kesef</i> (for there was no money). Rabbi Moses said: For <b>gamor amar</b> is like <b>im gamru va'avru nechamotav</b> (if His consolations have ceased and passed). And in my opinion: <b>gamor amar</b> — that He decreed that He will forsake me forever."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 77, :notes {0 "Rabbi Moses likely refers to Ibn Ezra's younger contemporary Moses ha-Kohen; the specific work or passage is not identified here."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:46.913150637Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}